#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096291 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7578c48-cc9e-5170-8ffe-5ebee6580677" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Decimals in One Equation"}] :question/id #uuid "0a5391bf-06ef-5099-a835-0375ff96c342" :question/math-academy-id "e-1038" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n${0.5x + 3y + 4 = 0; 4x =-20y - 20$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the first equation by $10$, as follows:\n\n$$\n{0.5x + 3y + 4 = 0 \\mid \\mid \\cdot 10; 4x =-20y - 20\n$$\n\nWe also notice that each equation can be simplified by dividing by a common factor. In the first equation, the common factor is $5$, while in the second equation, the common factor is $4$.\n\n$$\n{5x + 30y + 40 = 0 \\mid \\mid \\div 5; 4x =-20y - 20 \\mid \\mid \\div 4\n$$\n\nNotice that the second equation is already solved for $x$. So, we can substitute $x = -5y-5$ into the first equation and then solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx + 6y + 8 &= 0 \\\\\n(-5y - 5) + 6y + 8 &= 0 \\\\\ny + 3 &= 0 \\\\\ny &= -3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $x$, we substitute $y=-3$ back into $x=-5y-5$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &= -5y - 5 \\\\\n&=-5(-3) - 5 \\\\\n&= 15 - 5 \\\\\n&= 10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x = 10$ and $y = -3$, which can be expressed as $(10, -3)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096292 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc62d8df-450f-5f7a-b647-b53c051f8339" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Decimals in Both Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "8f4b321d-ebc7-5f78-9bde-b51b297a0cc0" :question/math-academy-id "e-1039" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n${1.4x + 2.8y = 1.4; 0.02x + 0.01y = 0.05$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the first equation by $10$ and the second equation by $100$, as follows:\n\n$$\n{1.4x + 2.8y = 1.4 \\mid \\mid \\cdot 10; 0.02x + 0.01y = 0.05 \\mid \\mid \\cdot 100\n$$\n\nTo simplify the first equation, we divide by $14$:\n\n$$\n{14x + 28y = 14 \\mid \\mid \\div 14; 2x + y = 5\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Notice that the first equation can easily be solved for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx + 2y &= 1 \\\\\nx &= 1 - 2y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can substitute $x=1-2y$ into the second equation and then solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x + y &= 5 \\\\\n2(1 - 2y) + y &= 5 \\\\\n2 - 4y + y &= 5 \\\\\n2 - 3y &= 5 \\\\\n- 3y &= 3 \\\\\ny &= -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $x$, we substitute $y=-1$ back into $x=1-2y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &= 1 - 2y \\\\\n&= 1 - 2(-1) \\\\\n&= 1 + 2 \\\\\n&= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x =3$ and $y =-1$, which can be expressed as $(3, -1)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252645 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7578c48-cc9e-5170-8ffe-5ebee6580677" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Decimals in One Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50fba200-cc50-59ff-8e9d-08ef5d1a4c5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252647} {:answer/id #uuid "9bd2c871-f376-54ed-a302-50068a27509b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252648} {:answer/id #uuid "2bb080ff-07ac-5d16-acdd-b55afe508236" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252649} {:answer/id #uuid "cc2d7656-46cf-54bb-95e6-7bb2fa44ef8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252650} {:answer/id #uuid "cf3d11c1-9f99-5daf-8b7c-e595c728786f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bd2c871-f376-54ed-a302-50068a27509b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252648} :answer-field/id #uuid "feb69340-ddff-558d-8d5a-1d96eaac1c2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252646}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "57dc1d54-5a8e-5211-85bd-cc10abc48676" :question/math-academy-id "q-112561" :question/problem "Let $(x,y)$ be the solution of the following system. What is the value of $x+y?$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=7 \\\\ 0.5x+0.4y=0.2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the second equation by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=7 &  \\\\ 0.5x+0.4y=0.2 & |\\,\\times 10\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=7 \\\\ 5x+4y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we multiply the  first equation by $-5,$ then we will get a $-5x$ term that can cancel with the $5x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=7 & |\\,\\times (-5) \\\\ 5x+4y=2\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}-5x-15y=-35 \\\\ 5x+4y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $x$-variable and allows us to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-\\cancel{5x}-15y & =-35 \\\\ \\cancel{5x}+4y & =2 \\\\ (-15y+4y) & =(-33) \\\\ -11y & =-33 \\\\ y & =3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $y=3$ into the equation $x+3y=7$ to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}x+3y & =7 \\\\ x+3(3) & =7 \\\\ x+9 & =7 \\\\ x & =-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-2,\\,y=3.$ So,\n\n$$\nx+y=(-2)+(3)=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252652 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7578c48-cc9e-5170-8ffe-5ebee6580677" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Decimals in One Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eabc0142-7eb0-5ab1-a6eb-326228eab211" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252654} {:answer/id #uuid "c518d676-877a-5964-8421-6f3a90f5c6e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252655} {:answer/id #uuid "05fc0b25-f74c-5d87-a779-d8b41c5534d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252656} {:answer/id #uuid "5e307926-f7a3-5437-926b-44454610bbb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252657} {:answer/id #uuid "2204fa56-bedf-5d47-b318-62452e053e93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252658}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05fc0b25-f74c-5d87-a779-d8b41c5534d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252656} :answer-field/id #uuid "da0e2c83-9ad7-5d96-b0eb-34a56e7f4d98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252653}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "98c374fa-24fb-51fc-a983-bcd8e729a379" :question/math-academy-id "q-112562" :question/problem "Let $(x,y)$ be the solution of the following system. What is the value of $x+y?$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+3y=15 \\\\ 0.6x-0.8y=1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the second equation by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+3y=15 &  \\\\ 0.6x-0.8y=1 & |\\,\\times 10\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}4x+3y=15 \\\\ 6x-8y=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we multiply the first equation by $3$ and the second equation by $-2,$ we will get a $12x$ term in the first equation that can cancel with the $-12x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+3y=15 & |\\,\\times 3 \\\\ 6x-8y=10 & |\\,\\times -2\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}12x+9y=45 \\\\ -12x+16y=-20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $x$-variable and allows us to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{12x}+9y & =45 \\\\ -\\cancel{12x}+16y & =-20 \\\\ (9y+16y) & =(45-20) \\\\ 25y & =25 \\\\ y & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $y=1$ into the equation $4x+3y=15$ to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+3y & =15 \\\\ 4x+3 & =15 \\\\ 4x & =15-3 \\\\ 4x & =12 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $x=3$ and $y=1.$ So, \n\n$$\nx+y=3+1=4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252659 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc62d8df-450f-5f7a-b647-b53c051f8339" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Decimals in Both Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dce6ddb-77c5-5ad1-924a-02940711203d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252661} {:answer/id #uuid "b332a031-a486-55b5-be60-853913911c37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252662} {:answer/id #uuid "45a51123-3eb7-55a9-961b-64155e846ea8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252663} {:answer/id #uuid "95391b72-80cc-5413-890d-5e767afbded9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252664} {:answer/id #uuid "39171937-a4e5-5f88-9566-13de0c95c575" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39171937-a4e5-5f88-9566-13de0c95c575" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252665} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1b8d38f-f17e-5b5e-9bbc-04881cbd3213" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252660}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c910bf18-c47e-55bc-8cc2-bd689ff5d040" :question/math-academy-id "q-112564" :question/problem "Let $(a,b)$ be the solution of the following system. What is the value of $a+b?$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}a+1.5b-6=0 \\\\ 0.6a-0.4b-1=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply both equations by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}a+1.5b-6=0 & |\\,\\times 10 \\\\ 0.6a-0.4b-1=0 & |\\,\\times 10\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}10a+15b-60=0 \\\\ 6a-4b-10=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we  multiply the first equation by $\\frac{2}{5}$ and the second equation by $\\frac{3}{2},$ we will get a $6b$ term in the first equation that can cancel with the $-6b$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}10a+15b-60=0 & |\\,\\times \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ 6a-4b-10=0 & |\\,\\times \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}4a+6b-24=0 \\\\ 9a-6b-15=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $b$-variable and allows us to solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4a+\\cancel{6b}-24 & =0 \\\\ 9a-\\cancel{6b}-15 & =0 \\\\ (4a+9a)+(-24-15) & =0 \\\\ 13a-39 & =0 \\\\ a & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $a=3$ into the equation $6a-4b-10=0$ to solve for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6a-4b-10 & =0 \\\\ 6(3)-4b-10 & =0 \\\\ 18-4b-10 & =0 \\\\ 8-4b & =0 \\\\ b & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $a=3$ and $b=2.$ So, \n\n$$\na+b=3+2=5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252666 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7578c48-cc9e-5170-8ffe-5ebee6580677" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Decimals in One Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a565977-2287-518b-8c2d-94568532dbf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0.5,\\,b=-1.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252668} {:answer/id #uuid "175c6f1a-479f-5dde-9299-74ec7dfd10e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1.5,\\,b=2.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252669} {:answer/id #uuid "be36a7c0-12c8-5acd-8f3f-1bb2aeacacb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1.2,\\,b=1.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252670} {:answer/id #uuid "f7d33353-f1b6-5902-b2a5-3199f6f564a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-1.2,\\,b=0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252671} {:answer/id #uuid "517f2e68-a29f-5543-bc82-64db583b6526" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0.2,\\,b=1.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be36a7c0-12c8-5acd-8f3f-1bb2aeacacb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1.2,\\,b=1.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252670} :answer-field/id #uuid "17e32d48-05f2-5c8b-b27d-682fc71fd79c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252667}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8748ba37-2d9a-5451-b497-621aa22378b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-18688" :question/problem "Find the solution of the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}b=2a-1 \\\\ 1.5a+0.5b=2.5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the second equation by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}b=2a-1 &  \\\\ 1.5a+0.5b=2.5 & |\\,\\times 10\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}b=2a-1 \\\\ 15a+5b=25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the first equation is already solved for $b:$\n\n$$\nb=2a-1\n$$\n\nNow, to find the value of $a,$ we can substitute $b=2a-1$ into the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15a+5(2a-1) & =25 \\\\ 15a+10a-5 & =25 \\\\ 25a & =30 \\\\ a & =\\frac{30}{25} \\\\ a & =1.2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $a=1.2$ into the  first equation to get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =2(1.2)-1 \\\\  & =2.4-1 \\\\  & =1.4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $a=1.2$ and $b=1.4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252673 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7578c48-cc9e-5170-8ffe-5ebee6580677" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Decimals in One Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81751c11-386c-55d9-8ddc-79036db151c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252675} {:answer/id #uuid "ca0e3238-5f47-505a-b6b2-ec1b087aa0d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252676} {:answer/id #uuid "88ec735e-c235-5bae-b747-ecf2b7c29ecd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252677} {:answer/id #uuid "043eba32-079f-5541-bf70-5feec0fae366" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252678} {:answer/id #uuid "1a1dd514-544a-55c9-a2aa-99e818b740ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "043eba32-079f-5541-bf70-5feec0fae366" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252678} :answer-field/id #uuid "cddf50a8-a4b3-542e-bb60-d38d89bb54b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252674}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f271da85-4c2f-5548-b34e-bfcbc915419e" :question/math-academy-id "q-18702" :question/problem "Let $(x,y)$ be the solution of the following system. What is the value of $x-y?$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2.3x+4.6y=69 \\\\ 10x-20y=100\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the top equation by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2.3x+4.6y=69 & |\\,\\times 10 \\\\ 10x-20y=100 & \\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}23x+46y=690 \\\\ 10x-20y=100\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we divide the first equation by $23$ and the second equation by $10,$ we will get a $2y$ term in the first equation that can cancel with the $-2y$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}23x+46y=690 & |\\,÷23 \\\\ 10x-20y=100 & |\\,÷10\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=30 \\\\ x-2y=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $y$-variable and allows us to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+\\cancel{2y} & =30 \\\\ x-\\cancel{2y} & =10 \\\\ (x+x) & =(30+10) \\\\ 2x & =40 \\\\ x & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $x=20$ into the equation $x+2y=30$ to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2y & =30 \\\\ (20)+2y & =30 \\\\ 2y & =30-20 \\\\ 2y & =10 \\\\ y & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $x=20$ and $y=5.$ So, \n\n$$\nx-y=20-(5)=15.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252680 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc62d8df-450f-5f7a-b647-b53c051f8339" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Decimals in Both Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "435e1f44-ee49-53a1-949b-55d256fc75d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252682} {:answer/id #uuid "526622a4-637e-525a-b1ba-68a009ebc175" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252683} {:answer/id #uuid "95337147-3f23-562d-b3c0-f508168a3c6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252684} {:answer/id #uuid "12e38895-bd61-59cb-bc21-38804f861111" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252685} {:answer/id #uuid "afde4537-0447-5bd5-9358-fce72150f84b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252686}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "526622a4-637e-525a-b1ba-68a009ebc175" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252683} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8962d05-7e6a-5a7e-926b-dabbe183c86e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252681}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b71e530d-e775-501c-9fa4-f49030e390f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-18720" :question/problem "Let $(p,q)$ be the solution of the following system. What is the value of $p+2q?$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0.36p+1.2q=0.36 \\\\ -1.9p-7.6q=3.8\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the first equation by $100$ and the second equation by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0.36p+1.2q=0.36 & |\\times 100 \\\\ -1.9p-7.6q=3.8 & |\\times 10\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}36p+120q=36 \\\\ -19p-76q=38\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we can solve for $p$ in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-19p-76q & =38 \\\\ -19p & =76q+38 \\\\ p & =\\frac{76q+38}{-19} \\\\ p & =-4q-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the value of $q,$ we can substitute $p=-4q-2$ into the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}36p+120q & =36 \\\\ 36(-4q-2)+120q & =36 \\\\ -144q-72+120q & =36 \\\\ -24q & =108 \\\\ q & =-\\frac{108}{24} \\\\ q & =-4.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $q=-4.5$ into the equation $p=-4q-2$ to get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =-4q-2 \\\\ p & =-4(-4.5)-2 \\\\ p & =18-2 \\\\ p & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $p=16$ and $q=-4.5.$ So, \n\n$$\np+2q=16+2(-4.5)=16-9=7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252687 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7578c48-cc9e-5170-8ffe-5ebee6580677" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Decimals in One Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82eb724a-0359-51da-a10b-3d63bb256e18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0.5,\\,b=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252689} {:answer/id #uuid "c2832ded-941c-51ca-ba7d-742114b4c176" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-1,\\,b=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252690} {:answer/id #uuid "8306b4ac-e73a-5f0c-b5fa-0dafef23d730" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-0.5,\\,b=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252691} {:answer/id #uuid "24bca577-e126-5638-9da3-2ed680242cd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252692} {:answer/id #uuid "67617072-84e3-53c7-96a3-035c1bf54f6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8306b4ac-e73a-5f0c-b5fa-0dafef23d730" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-0.5,\\,b=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252691} :answer-field/id #uuid "50bfc997-fa11-5146-ae99-59a1bd6981aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252688}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ec708ad2-0528-5c6b-a4f1-9dab6fa5292e" :question/math-academy-id "q-18827" :question/problem "Find the solution of the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}12.8a+6.4=-6.4b \\\\ 2a+1=b\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the first equation by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}12.8a+6.4=-6.4b & |\\,\\times 10 \\\\ 2a+1=b & \\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}128a+64=-64b \\\\ 2a+1=b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the second equation is already solved for $b:$\n\n$$\nb=2a+1\n$$\n\nNow, to find the value of $a,$ we can substitute $b=2a+1$ into the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}128a+64 & =-64b \\\\ 128a+64 & =-64(2a+1) \\\\ 128a+64 & =-128a-64 \\\\ 256a & =-128 \\\\ a & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ a & =-0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $a=-0.5$ into the second equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a+1 & =b \\\\ 2(-0.5)+1 & =b \\\\ -1+1 & =b \\\\ b & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-0.5$ and $b=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252694 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc62d8df-450f-5f7a-b647-b53c051f8339" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Decimals in Both Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bea154a-0961-5d9f-8b44-5d5366c31f6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$v=-75,$ $w=-170$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252696} {:answer/id #uuid "ee3cfdfa-0bad-5ac9-8f20-e6c0cc73406e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$v=0,$ $w=-20$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252697} {:answer/id #uuid "54582aaf-16c4-5547-9138-a7fe1bb1a4b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$v=50,$ $w=80$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252698} {:answer/id #uuid "446ebbac-38c1-54e0-b482-d681af127503" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$v=-50,$ $w=-120$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252699} {:answer/id #uuid "b538716a-5edf-5471-8c28-95a00972207a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$v=25,$ $w=30$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252700}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bea154a-0961-5d9f-8b44-5d5366c31f6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$v=-75,$ $w=-170$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252696} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6192324-5003-5119-9a67-ea2ffe996700" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252695}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3af04ac3-aff2-5a62-a4f3-e410d24890bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-18831" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0.09v-0.04w=0.05 \\\\ 0.02v-0.01w=0.2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply both equations by $100,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0.09v-0.04w=0.05 & |\\times 100 \\\\ 0.02v-0.01w=0.2 & |\\times 100\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}9v-4w=5 \\\\ 2v-w=20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we multiply the second equation by $-4,$ we will get a $4w$ term that can cancel with the $-4w$ term in the first equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}9v-4w=5 &  \\\\ 2v-w=20 & |\\,\\times (-4)\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}9v-4w=5 \\\\ -8v+4w=-80\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $w$-variable and allows us to solve for $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9v-\\cancel{4w} & =5 \\\\ -8v+\\cancel{4w} & =-80 \\\\ (9v-8v) & =(5-80) \\\\ v & =-75\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $v=-75$ into the equation $2v-w=20$ to solve for $w:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2v-w & =20 \\\\ 2(-75)-w & =20 \\\\ -150-w & =20 \\\\ -w & =170 \\\\ w & =-170\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $v=-75,\\,w=-170.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252701 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc62d8df-450f-5f7a-b647-b53c051f8339" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Decimals in Both Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8635826a-9330-5f5c-989a-b191eac68ff6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252703} {:answer/id #uuid "6a88a648-90b2-5754-9b51-efb0ab983224" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252704} {:answer/id #uuid "3cc72e39-e5d9-5c68-b1d0-8aa36d554cc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252705} {:answer/id #uuid "0158c616-cb2f-5e32-af59-5b48a43c9810" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252706} {:answer/id #uuid "487e7e86-c64d-5013-9120-349863e41031" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a88a648-90b2-5754-9b51-efb0ab983224" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252704} :answer-field/id #uuid "30c70cfc-4394-59f8-a13e-057991ac0dfa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252702}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c87ad3c5-91fd-58f1-b98c-7515580415bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-18853" :question/problem "Let $(v,w)$ be the solution of the following system. What is the value of $v+w?$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0.5v-2.5w=7.5 \\\\ 0.7v+0.3w=2.9\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply both equations by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0.5v-2.5w=7.5 & |\\times 10 \\\\ 0.7v+0.3w=2.9 & |\\times 10\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}5v-25w=75 \\\\ 7v+3w=29\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we can solve for $v$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5v-25w & =75 \\\\ 5v & =25w+75 \\\\ v & =\\frac{25w+75}{5} \\\\ v & =5w+15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the value of $w,$ we can substitute $v=5w+15$ into the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7v+3w & =29 \\\\ 7(5w+15)+3w & =29 \\\\ 35w+105+3w & =29 \\\\ 38w & =-76 \\\\ w & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $w=-2$ into the equation $v=5w+15$ to get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =5w+15 \\\\ v & =5(-2)+15 \\\\ v & =-10+15 \\\\ v & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $v=5,\\,w=-2.$ So,\n\n$$\nv+w=5+(-2)=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252708 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc62d8df-450f-5f7a-b647-b53c051f8339" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System Containing Decimals in Both Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dde04b4-25e8-55ed-afe9-fda0403c4729" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=\\frac{4}{3},$ $y=-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252710} {:answer/id #uuid "06c74088-0ffe-53af-898c-82f752b76c78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=1,$ $y=-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252711} {:answer/id #uuid "f2a3a49f-dfa9-5c2c-9f37-0bc9132a8eb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=\\frac{7}{3},$ $y=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252712} {:answer/id #uuid "4a07a067-9855-5e91-93a1-f1bc495b21db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=2,$ $y=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252713} {:answer/id #uuid "9772418c-1188-5457-bb21-5aa43d1014fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=\\frac{5}{3},$ $y=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252714}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9772418c-1188-5457-bb21-5aa43d1014fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=\\frac{5}{3},$ $y=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252714} :answer-field/id #uuid "10936f57-bd98-5481-94b8-cd4228f57c8a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252709}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3d7c59ff-df86-5863-a05a-c20fb84b2ead" :question/math-academy-id "q-26223" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0.3x-0.1y=0.6 \\\\ 0.6x+0.8y=0.2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply both equations by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0.3x-0.1y=0.6 & |\\,\\times 10 \\\\ 0.6x+0.8y=0.2 & |\\,\\times 10\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}3x-y=6 \\\\ 6x+8y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that if we divide the second equation by $(-2),$ we will get a $-3x$ term in the second equation that can cancel with the $3x$ term in the first equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-y=6 &  \\\\ 6x+8y=2 & |\\,÷(-2)\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}3x-y=6 \\\\ -3x-4y=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $x$-variable and allows us to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{3x}-y & =6 \\\\ -\\cancel{3x}-4y & =-1 \\\\ (-y-4y) & =(6-1) \\\\ -5y & =5 \\\\ y & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $y=-1$ into the equation $3x-y=6$ to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-y & =6 \\\\ 3x-(-1) & =6 \\\\ 3x & =5 \\\\ x & =\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $x=\\frac{5}{3}$ and $y=-1.$"}]}
